// Quoted: the label contains a space.
//
// The same BI_ALPHA constant as `alpha` above — it appears twice in the mode
// table, at index 4 and index 11 (wz3_bitmap_ops.ops:683) — plus a trailing
// `out->PreMulAlpha()` for index 11 only (:706).
//
// So the two are not a duplicate but a PAIR, and knowing what BI_ALPHA is for
// makes the pairing obvious: "attach an alpha channel", and "attach one and
// premultiply it" — the second being the form compositing hardware usually wants.
// The checksums differ, and now it is clear why they should.
//
// Correct: as merge_alpha, with the RGB scaled down by the alpha it just gained.
// Against src_ramp that shows as `b 182, g 182, r 182, a 195` where merge_alpha
// gave `b 0, g 0, r 0, a 195` — so unlike merge_alpha, this one differs from its
// input even in `rgb` mode, which is the cheapest way to tell the pair apart.
op GenBitmap.Merge at 77,1 size 6x1 {
  name = merge_premul
  Mode = "premul alpha"
}
